# Defense-in-depth for Windows CI (2026-09-28 windows-latest fixture-test investigation): the
# speech-rate/bad Windows CI failure turned out to be a path/URL bug in speech-rate.mjs itself (see
# that file's own comment), NOT CRLF — a local `git -c core.autocrlf=true clone` repro showed every
# fixture, including speech-rate's, still parses and verdicts correctly under CRLF line endings.
# Even so, this repo shipped with no .gitattributes at all, which leaves every text fixture's line
# endings up to each contributor's/runner's global git config (autocrlf) by accident rather than by
# design — a real risk for any *future* gate that does something more line-sensitive than this one
# turned out to need. Pin it explicitly instead of relying on that being true forever.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fixture "audio" files are tiny synthetic placeholders (a few bytes), not real MP3/WAV — mark them
# binary explicitly so line-ending normalization never touches them regardless of git's own
# content-sniffing heuristic (they already contain a NUL byte, so the heuristic catches them today,
# but the point of this file is to stop depending on heuristics for anything that must stay binary).
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.mp4 binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
